<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ebrohimi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ebrohimi was the fortified town of the Itsekiri merchant and governor of the river <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nana-olomu">Nana Olomu</a>, on a creek of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> River in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-delta">Niger Delta</a>. From there <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanaya">Nana</a> controlled the palm-oil trade between the interior and European firms. In 1894 forces of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> Coast <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> besieged and destroyed the town after weeks of fighting, and Nana was later sent into exile.</p></div>
